---
title: Mulled wine
servings: 6
tags: [cocktail, wine, christmas, winter]
time: 25 minutes
source: Mulled Wine by Once Upon a Chef, https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/mulled-wine.html
---

In a #large saucepan{}(stainless steel or enamel), put @red wine{750%ml}(dry), @orange{1}(thinly sliced), @brandy{1/4%cup}, @honey{3%tbsp}, @granulated sugar{2%tbsp}, @cinnamon sticks{2}, @whole cloves{6}, @star anise{2}(whole pods) and @fresh ginger{1}(1-inch piece, peeled and thinly sliced). Warm over medium-low heat ~{15%minutes} to 20 minutes without letting it bubble. Taste, and add more honey, sugar or brandy if you like. Strain into a #heatproof pitcher{} or straight into #mugs{}, and serve warm.

> It keeps 3 days in the fridge. Reheat gently on the stove or in a slow cooker.
